This manual presents the Möbius 8 system as a series of modular upgrades, each building on the previous to create a cohesive, fractal-based AI ecosystem. We start with base hardware setup and progressively add layers for core logic, AI core, UI, ethics, ML modules, biofeedback, community mesh, and full integration. Assumptions: You're using a Raspberry Pi (e.g., Pi 4/5) as Tinybox; Python 3.12+ for backend; Node.js for frontend/UI. Steps are practical, drawn from standard practices for AI/ML on edge devices.

Upgrade 0: Base Hardware and OS Setup (Tinybox Foundation)
Prerequisites: Raspberry Pi board (4/5 recommended for ML), microSD card (16GB+), power supply, optional case/cooling.
Insert microSD into computer; download Raspberry Pi OS (Lite for headless, Desktop for UI dev) from raspberrypi.com/software/operating-systems.
Use Raspberry Pi Imager tool (download from raspberrypi.com) to flash OS to SD card; enable SSH in advanced options for remote access.
Insert SD into Pi, power on; connect via Ethernet/WiFi (default user: pi, pass: raspberry—change immediately with passwd).
Update system: sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y.
Install essentials: sudo apt install git python3-pip python3-venv build-essential -y.
Config: Run sudo raspi-config to expand filesystem, enable VNC/SSH if needed, set locale/timezone.
Test: Reboot, SSH in (ssh pi@raspberrypi.local), verify Python (python3 --version).

Upgrade 1: Python Environment and Virtual Env (Core Development Setup)
Builds on: OS base for isolated code execution.
Create project dir: mkdir mobius8 && cd mobius8.
Create venv: python3 -m venv venv.
Activate: source venv/bin/activate (add to .bashrc for auto-activation if desired).
Upgrade pip: pip install --upgrade pip.
Install base libs: pip install numpy scipy sympy flask fastapi uvicorn requests.
Config: Add requirements.txt with pip freeze > requirements.txt for reproducibility.
Test: Run python -c "import numpy as np; print(np.__version__)" to verify.

